# Commit subject + category

When the user asks for a Git commit subject line (or message subject only), always include:

1. **Category** — one of: `feature`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `perf`, `security` (pick the best fit; use `fix` for bug/reliability remediations, `feature` for new user-facing capability, etc.)
2. **Subject** — concise imperative summary of *why* / outcome (same style as normal commit subjects)

Format the reply like:

```text
Category: fix
Subject: …
```

Do not invent a full commit body unless asked. Do not create the commit unless asked.
